Hi,<br><br>we're using Bullet as a DLL/SO in a plug-in framework, so we've done some work to make the C API work for us. For now, we're really just adding stuff how and when we need it, some stuff even on extensions in Bullet that we've written ourselves. <br><br>That being said, maybe it's useful to someone, and maybe we'll try and get this in the official release. Not anywhere near mature enough for that, though. <br><br>It's based on a modified version of Bullet 2.72. Source license: same as Bullet. File attached to this message.<br><br>Have fun!<br>- Daan Nusman<br>re-lion<dl class="file"><dt><span class="imageset icon_topic_attach"></span> <a class="postlink" href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/download/file.php?id=276">Bullet-C-API.zip</a></dt></dl><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2833">nebula</a> — Tue May 26, 2009 11:50 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
